{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "9548a068-b36f-4752-b2a0-721d806a8789",
		"name": "Node Redis API",
		"description": "Collection of endpoints for the Node.js app with Redis. Covers the happy path and the sad path (validation, auth, ownership, refresh-rotation/reuse-detection, logout-revocation, and RBAC errors) for every endpoint. Run with newman: `npm run test:collection`.\n\nNote: two happy-path cases are intentionally not covered here, both because they require reaching into the database directly, which is out of reach for a black-box HTTP collection — covered by the Jest e2e suite instead:\n- The 404 \"user not found\" case on GET /users/profile/:id (a true read-through cache; reaching it requires deleting the user from PostgreSQL directly).\n- The 200 happy path on GET /admin/users (there is no self-service way to become an admin — see the README's \"Roles & Access Control\" section — so only the 401/403 sad paths are covered here).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "43702418"
	},
